-- Manulife Vietnam term life product terms, row VN-11: the hostile reading. Each block shows, in
-- L4, the surprising answer a finding in NOTES.md section 4 describes. Every assertion here is
-- MEANT to pass: it pins the defect as the instrument has it. A rival reading that the encoding did
-- not take is defined here, beside the evidence, and nowhere else, so the rule modules carry only
-- the readings taken. Findings 7, 9, 11 and 14 are reading only and have no block.

§ `Finding 1 — Art 3(c)(i) names nobody as the one who commits the crime`

-- On the words, a death "directly or indirectly" resulting from "Phạm tội" is excluded whoever
-- committed the crime, so the insured who is murdered is excluded too. The encoding takes the
-- insured's own crime (fork F6); the literal reading is this rule.
@ref Art 3(c)(i), src:132-137
GIVEN `the death` IS A `The death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(c), on the literal reading — the death benefit is excluded for` `the death` MEANS
        "(i), anyone's crime" ... (`the death`'s `resulting directly or indirectly from the insured committing a crime, or intentionally committing a criminal offence`
                                   OR `the death`'s `resulting directly or indirectly from a crime committed by someone other than the insured`)
    OR  "(ii)"                ... `the death`'s `related to AIDS, an AIDS-related condition (ARC), or HIV infection`

-- The insured is killed in a robbery on 10 May 2023.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 3(c) — the death benefit is excluded for` (`a death from another person's crime on` (YMD 2023 5 10))
#ASSERT `Art 3(c), on the literal reading — the death benefit is excluded for` (`a death from another person's crime on` (YMD 2023 5 10))

§ `Finding 2 — "Phạm tội" has no intent in it`

-- The first limb of (i) is any crime; only the second says "intentionally". An insured who dies in
-- a crash caused by the insured's own careless driving, if that is a crime, is excluded: the
-- premium comes back less costs, 19 million, instead of 1 billion. Whether careless driving is a
-- crime is outside the document (the field records it as found).
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a death from the insured's own crime on` (YMD 2024 9 3))) EQUALS `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 3(c)" 19_000_000

§ `Finding 3 — only the policyholder can stop the claim year running`

-- The insured is also the policyholder and dies on 10 May 2023. The beneficiary learns of it only
-- on 1 December 2024 and claims at once. The policyholder is dead and cannot prove anything, and
-- the document gives the beneficiary no such right: the claim is out of time.
`a policyholder-insured's death, claimed by a beneficiary 19 months later` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `a signed application`,
                       (`The insured` WITH `true date of birth` IS YMD 1985 6 10, `resided in Vietnam on the issue date` IS TRUE, `also the policyholder` IS TRUE),
                       `premiums paid up`, `nothing undisclosed`, `no requests`, `a natural death on` (YMD 2023 5 10),
                       `a complete claim made on` (YMD 2024 12 1)
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` `a policyholder-insured's death, claimed by a beneficiary 19 months later` EQUALS `the claim for the death benefit is out of time`

§ `Finding 4 — the suicide years run from the issue date, not from the start of cover`

-- Effective 15 January 2020, issued 1 February 2020. A suicide on 20 January 2020, in force but
-- before issue, is not "within 2 years from" the issue date, so the full benefit is payable. A
-- suicide on 1 February 2022, two years and 17 days after cover began, is still inside.
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2020 1 20))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with` (`a suicide on` (YMD 2022 2 1))) EQUALS `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 11" 19_000_000

§ `Finding 5 — nothing is said about what is returned when the Company avoids the contract`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 10 — the premium returned when the Company treats the contract as void` BECAUSE "Art 10 does not say what is returned to the policyholder when the Company treats the contract as void"

§ `Finding 6 — no beneficiary, no answer`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the amounts paid to the beneficiaries in` (`the standard case with` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2023 5 10))) `no beneficiary designated` BECAUSE "Art 8 does not say who receives the death benefit when no beneficiary is designated"

§ `Finding 8 — a misstated Age undoes cover at any time, two-year limit or not`

-- Age misstated; the true Age at issue was 61. The insured dies in 2035, fifteen years after issue,
-- long after Art 10's two years. Art 9 has no time limit: the premium is refunded less costs, and
-- no death benefit is paid.
#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`A death claim` OF `the standard contract page`, `an application with the Age misstated`, `a resident insured born on` (YMD 1958 6 10), `premiums paid up`, `nothing undisclosed`, `no requests`, `a natural death on` (YMD 2035 3 3), `a complete claim made on` (YMD 2035 4 2)) EQUALS `no death benefit, and the premium is refunded` "Art 9" 19_000_000

§ `Finding 10 — conditions with no consequence, and one that a child cannot meet`

-- Art 1.3 admits an insured of Age 0; Art 1.5 requires the insured to sign the application, and
-- names nobody to sign for a child. On the record as a parent would truthfully give it (the insured
-- did not sign), the claim for a child is not answered.
`the layered child case, the insured not having signed` MEANS
    `A death claim` OF `the child's contract page`, `an application the insured did not sign`,
                       `a resident insured born on` (YMD 2021 3 1),
                       `premiums paid up`, `nothing undisclosed`,
                       (`The policyholder's requests` WITH `date the contract was received` IS YMD 2022 1 15, `date a written request to cancel was sent` IS NOTHING, `date the policyholder requested termination` IS NOTHING),
                       `a natural death on` (YMD 2023 12 20), `a complete claim made on` (YMD 2024 1 5)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of the death claim` `the layered child case, the insured not having signed` BECAUSE "Art 1.5 does not say what follows when the application was not signed by both the policyholder and the insured"

§ `Finding 12 — the free-look period is 14 days, and a refund is lost for want of receipts`

-- Received 5 February 2020; a request sent on 25 February 2020, the 20th day, is late under Art 4
-- (Law 08/2022/QH15 Art 35 gives 21 days: LAW fork L1). A request in time with the receipts not
-- returned refunds nothing, and no period is set for returning them.
#ASSERT `Art 4 — the result of the request to cancel` (`a request to cancel a contract received on 5 February 2020, sent on` (YMD 2020 2 25) `, receipts returned` TRUE) EQUALS `not cancelled under Art 4: the request was late`
#ASSERT `Art 4 — the result of the request to cancel` (`a request to cancel a contract received on 5 February 2020, sent on` (YMD 2020 2 10) `, receipts returned` FALSE) EQUALS `cancelled, and nothing is refunded`

§ `Finding 13 — "all premiums unpaid" against "will not require" the rest of the year`

-- Death on 10 May 2023 under a monthly mode: nothing overdue, 7.5 million of the year's premium
-- not yet due. The reading taken (fork F7) deducts nothing. Read literally,
-- "Tất cả các khoản phí bảo hiểm chưa đóng" deducts the 7.5 million that Art 5 says the Company
-- will not require.
`premiums paid monthly, 7.5 million of the year not yet due` MEANS
    `The premium record` WITH
        `first premium paid`                                    IS TRUE
        `instalment in default`                                 IS NOTHING
        `premiums due and unpaid at the death`                  IS 0
        `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`  IS 7_500_000
        `total premium paid`                                    IS 20_000_000
        `total premium payable at the true Age and sex`         IS 20_000_000
        `reasonable costs and expenses deducted by the Company` IS 1_000_000
        `date of the most recent reinstatement`                 IS NOTHING

@ref Art 3(a)(iii), src:93; Art 5, src:162-169
GIVEN `the record` IS A `The premium record`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 3(a)(iii), on the literal reading — every premium not yet paid` `the record` MEANS
        `the record`'s `premiums due and unpaid at the death`
    PLUS `the record`'s `premiums of the policy year not yet due at the death`

#ASSERT `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with premiums` `premiums paid monthly, 7.5 million of the year not yet due` `and the death` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2023 5 10))) EQUALS `the death benefit is payable` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 1_000_000_000 37 0 (`Art 3(a)(iii), on the literal reading — every premium not yet paid` `premiums paid monthly, 7.5 million of the year not yet due`) EQUALS 992_500_000

§ `Finding 15 — before the first premium, no rule`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the outcome of the death claim` (`the standard case with premiums` `no premium paid` `and the death` (`a natural death on` (YMD 2020 3 1))) BECAUSE "Art 5 does not say whether the contract is in force before the first premium is paid"

§ `Finding 16 — the death benefit has no floor`

-- (i) plus (ii) less (iii), with nothing to stop it below nil: a child of Age 0, a sum insured of
-- 100 million (20% is 20 million), 25 million overdue. Theoretical: premiums so large against the
-- sum insured are not realistic.
#ASSERT `Art 3(a) — the death benefit` 100_000_000 0 0 25_000_000 EQUALS 0 MINUS 5_000_000
